{"evt":"note_created","id":"note-mqfm5mvl8zw","workspace":"/Users/imyu/Desktop/zonoid","title":"judge next route is workspace blind over HTTP","summary":"For the SWE-Bench-CL adapter: GET /judge/next (both eager ?node= and the global cursor queue) reads state.overlay / state.workspace HARDCODED in routes/judge.js — it ignores the workspace query param. So an isolated per-sequence eval workspace CANNOT read its autowired candidate edge set or pending-dup clusters over HTTP. POST /judge/verdict IS workspace-targetable (targetOverlay). Bridge: the adapter drives the judge WITHOUT reading the queue, using the {note_key, match.key} the POST /overlay/note response returns on a dup-guard fire — it posts a markDistinct verdict (clears pending_dup so the provisional note becomes recall-visible) plus a keepEdge for the autowired note to its match. Two gotchas: (1) markDistinct/markJudged are NOT in the /judge/verdict bare-body fallback allowlist (routes/judge.js line ~132) — they MUST be wrapped as {verdicts:[{markDistinct:...}]} or applied is a silent no-op; (2) the dup guard fires at cosine>=0.70, so consecutive similar CL experiences land pending_dup invisible until judged — a flat force:true store hid this entirely.","created_by":"main","valid_from":"2026-06-15T19:35:57.969Z","vec":[-0.14235585927963257,0.011351221241056919,-0.03624778613448143,0.003520477330312133,0.07003842294216156,0.016535770148038864,0.028051845729351044,0.010672868229448795,0.03492152318358421,-0.007292976602911949,0.02945195697247982,0.011071346700191498,0.011711959727108479,-0.037974026054143906,-0.02792203053832054,0.0720858946442604,0.08203266561031342,-0.025949981063604355,0.01716809906065464,-0.015319112688302994,0.07461763173341751,0.0030178900342434645,0.05110861733555794,-0.049438439309597015,-0.07546903938055038,-0.00286231585778296,-0.09257206320762634,0.020225021988153458,0.016637172549962997,-0.07547326385974884,0.0020825567189604044,0.005831588059663773,-0.12813422083854675,0.012014372